          %h3#remark_2 Remark
          %p
            Whereas, general
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+geometric+morphisms"} open morphisms
            are only bound to preserve
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/first+order+logic"} first order logic
            %em inclusions
            preserve also
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+order+logic"} higher order logic
            since their
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inverse+image"} inverse images
            are logical.
          %p
            That the inverse image is logical is a special case of the general fact that the pullback functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℰ
                  %mo →
                  %mi ℰ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}\to\mathcal{E}/X
            along
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X\to 1
            is logical for arbitrary objects
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Sh
                      %mrow
                        %mi o
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi U
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ℰ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≅
                    %mi ℰ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sh_{o(U)}(\mathcal{E})\cong\mathcal{E}/U
          %h2#open_localizations Open localizations
          %p
            Subtoposes of a topos
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℰ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}
            correspond to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/localization"} localizations
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℰ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}
            i.e. replete, reflective subcategories whose reflector preserves finite limits. Just as this notion makes sense more generally for categories with finite limits, the notion of open localization makes sense more generally for
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+presentable+category"} locally presentable categories
          %p
            Given a locally
            = succeed "-presentable" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi α
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
            with subcategory of
            = succeed "-presentable" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi α
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒫
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{P}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Ω
                    %mi 𝒞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega_\mathcal{C}
            of the subobject classifier of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi Set
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi 𝒫
                        %mi op
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set^{\mathcal{P}^{op}}
            given by
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Ω
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi P
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %mo =
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega_\mathcal{C}(P):=
            set of
            = succeed "-exact" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi α
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒫
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mtext _
                    %mo ,
                    %mi P
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{P}(\text{_},P)
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
            correspond to topologies
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi j
                    %mo :
                    %msub
                      %mi Ω
                      %mi 𝒞
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi Ω
                      %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j:\Omega_\mathcal{C}\to\Omega_\mathcal{C}
          %p
            At this level of generality, an open subtopos of a Grothendieck topos corresponds to the notion of an
            %strong open localization
            of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+presentable+category"} locally presentable category
            that is studied in
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#BK91"} Borceux-Korotenski (1991)
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_3 Proposition
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi l
                    %mo ⊣
                    %mi i
                    %mo :
                    %mi 𝒟
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} l\dashv i: \mathcal{D}\hookrightarrow\mathcal{C}
              be a localization of a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+presentable+category"} locally presentable category
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝒞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
              %em open
              if the following equivalent conditions are satisfied:
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  The corresponding
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closure+operator"} closure operator
                  admits a universal dense interior operator.
              %li
                %p
                  The associated
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lawvere-Tierney+topology"} topology
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi j
                          %mi 𝒟
                        %mo :
                        %msub
                          %mi Ω
                          %mi 𝒞
                        %mo →
                        %msub
                          %mi Ω
                          %mi 𝒞
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j_\mathcal{D}:\Omega_\mathcal{C}\to\Omega_\mathcal{C}
                  has a left adjoint.
              %li
                %p
                  The localization is
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/essential+geometric+morphism"} essential
                  with
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi k
                        %mo ⊣
                        %mi l
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k\dashv l
                  and, additionally, the first of the following diagrams
                  %sup#fnref:1
                    %a{:href => "#fn:1", :rel => "footnote"} 1
                  being a pullback implies the second being a pullback, too:
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi D
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mi d
                          %mtd
                            %mi D
                            %mo ′
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi f
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                            %mi p
                            %mo .
                            %mi b
                            %mo .
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                            %mi g
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi lC
                          %mtd
                            %munder
                              %mo →
                              %mi lc
                          %mtd
                            %mi lC
                            %mo ′
                    %mspace{:width => "2em"}
                    %mo ⇒
                    %mspace{:width => "2em"}
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi kD
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mi kd
                          %mtd
                            %mi kD
                            %mo ′
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mi f
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                            %mi p
                            %mo .
                            %mi b
                            %mo .
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                            %mover
                              %mi g
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi C
                          %mtd
                            %munder
                              %mo →
                              %mi c
                          %mtd
                            %mi C
                            %mo ′
                    %mspace{:width => "1em"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    D&amp;\overset{d}{\to}&amp;D'\\
                    f\downarrow&amp;p.b.&amp;\downarrow g\\
                    lC&amp;\underset{lc}{\to}&amp;lC'
                    }
                    
                    \\qquad\Rightarrow
                    \\qquad
                    
                    \\array{
                    kD&amp;\overset{kd}{\to}&amp;kD'\\
                    \\bar{f}\downarrow&amp;p.b.&amp;\downarrow \bar{g}\\
                    C&amp;\underset{c}{\to}&amp;C'
                    }\quad .
          %p
            In case
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
            is a topos,
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi i
                  %mo :
                  %mi 𝒟
                  %mo ↪
                  %mi 𝒞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i:\mathcal{D}\hookrightarrow\mathcal{C}
            is an open subtopos.
          %p
            Open localizations are special cases of
            = succeed "," do
              %strong essential localizations
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_4 Proposition
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
              a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+presentable+category"} locally presentable category
          %p
            cf.
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#BK91"} Borceux-Korotenski (1991, p.235)
          #open_supremum.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_5 Proposition
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
              a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+presentable+category"} locally presentable category
              where unions are
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+colimit"} universal
          %p
            cf.
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#BK91"} Borceux-Korotenski (1991, p.236)
          %p This applies e.g. to Grothendieck toposes since they are locally presentable and colimits are universal.
          #open_supremum.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_6 Proposition
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
              a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+presentable+category"} locally presentable category
              where unions are
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+colimit"} universal
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
              constitute a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locale"} locale
          %p
            cf.
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#BK91"} Borceux-Korotenski (1991, p.237)
          %p
            The following proposition closes the circle and recovers the primordial example of sheaf subtoposes
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Sh
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sh(U)
            on open subsets
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
            as a special case:
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_7 Proposition
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
              a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+presentable+category"} locally presentable category
              in which colimits are
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+colimit"} universal
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locale"} locale
              of open localizations of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
              is isomorphic to the locale of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subterminal+object"} subterminal objects
              of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝒞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
          %p
            cf.
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#BK91"} Borceux-Korotenski (1991, p.238)
          %h2#ext_int Open subtoposes associated to a subtopos
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Sh
                    %mi j
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ℰ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ↪
                  %mi ℰ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sh_j(\mathcal{E})\hookrightarrow\mathcal{E}
            be a subtopos of a (Grothendieck) topos with corresponding
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lawvere-Tierney+topology"} topology
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi j
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j
            %a{:href => "#open_supremum"} prop.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#open_supremum"}
            it follows that the supremum of the family of all open subtoposes contained in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Sh
                    %mi j
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ℰ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sh_j(\mathcal{E})
            is open again and, since it coincides with the supremum in the lattice of all localizations, is contained in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Sh
                      %mi j
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ℰ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sh_j(\mathcal{E})
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Sh
                    %mi j
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ℰ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sh_j(\mathcal{E})
            and therefore called the
            %strong interior
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Sh
                      %mi j
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ℰ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sh_j(\mathcal{E})
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Sh
                    %mrow
                      %mi o
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi int
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi j
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ℰ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sh_{o(int(j))}(\mathcal{E})
            and the corresponding
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subterminal+object"} subterminal object
            by
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi int
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi j
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} int(j)
          %p
            Whereas the other open subtopos
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Sh
                    %mrow
                      %mi o
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi ext
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi j
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ℰ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sh_{o(ext(j))}(\mathcal{E})
            connected with
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Sh
                    %mi j
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ℰ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sh_j(\mathcal{E})
            corresponding to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ext
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi j
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ext(j)
            is the biggest open subtopos disjoint from
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Sh
                    %mi j
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ℰ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sh_j(\mathcal{E})
            i.e. its exterior. Then the sum
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Sh
                    %mrow
                      %mi o
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi ext
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi j
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ℰ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ∨
                  %msub
                    %mi Sh
                    %mrow
                      %mi o
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi int
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi j
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ℰ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sh_{o(ext(j))}(\mathcal{E}) \vee Sh_{o(int(j))}(\mathcal{E})
            is open again and corresponds to the subterminal object
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ext
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi j
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∨
                    %mi int
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi j
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ext(j)\vee int(j)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Sh
                    %mrow
                      %mi c
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi ext
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi j
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ∨
                      %mi int
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi j
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ℰ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sh_{c(ext(j)\vee int(j))}(\mathcal{E})
            is called the boundary of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Sh
                    %mi j
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ℰ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sh_j(\mathcal{E})
            in (
            %a{:href => "#SGA4"}> SGA 4
            , p. 461).
          %p
            For some further details see at
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dense+subtopos"} dense subtopos
